Message:
The core idea of **JSON serialization** is simple:  
You take a C# object → turn it into JSON text → optionally write it to a file or send it over the wire.

Below are **clean, practical examples** using both **System.Text.Json** (built‑in) and **Newtonsoft.Json** (classic). Each example is ready to paste into a Visual Studio console project.

---

## System.Text.Json — The Modern Built‑In Way

### 1. Serialize a Simple Object
```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person
{
    Name = "John Doe",
    Age = 30,
    IsStudent = false
};

string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person);
Console.WriteLine(json);
```

### 2. Serialize with Pretty Formatting
```csharp
var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    WriteIndented = true
};

string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options);
Console.WriteLine(json);
```

### 3. Serialize a List of Objects
```csharp
var people = new List<Person>
{
    new Person { Name = "Alice", Age = 25, IsStudent = true },
    new Person { Name = "Bob", Age = 40, IsStudent = false }
};

string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(people, new JsonSerializerOptions { WriteIndented = true });
Console.WriteLine(json);
```

### 4. Serialize and Write to a File
```csharp
File.WriteAllText("people.json", json);
```

---

## Newtonsoft.Json — The Flexible, Dynamic Way

### 1. Basic Serialization
```csharp
using Newtonsoft.Json;

var json = JsonConvert.SerializeObject(person);
Console.WriteLine(json);
```

### 2. Pretty Formatting
```csharp
var json = JsonConvert.SerializeObject(person, Formatting.Indented);
Console.WriteLine(json);
```

### 3. Serialize a Dictionary
```csharp
var dict = new Dictionary<string, int>
{
    { "apples", 5 },
    { "oranges", 3 }
};

string json = JsonConvert.SerializeObject(dict, Formatting.Indented);
Console.WriteLine(json);
```

### 4. Serialize Dynamic Objects
```csharp
dynamic obj = new
{
    Name = "Dynamic Dan",
    Skills = new[] { "C#", "JSON", "Azure" }
};

string json = JsonConvert.SerializeObject(obj, Formatting.Indented);
Console.WriteLine(json);
```

---

## The Person Class Used in Examples
```csharp
public class Person
{
    public string Name { get; set; }
    public int Age { get; set; }
    public bool IsStudent { get; set; }
}
```

